From 2c7bea9cc20f13fdedff03e513cfb87f3eef0edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heappi <heappi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:07:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] snapshot: chained checkpoints

JS_SNAPSHOT_CHAIN writes a delta of the current base and then makes the
state it describes the new base of the runtime, so the next checkpoint
only holds what changed since this one. The header of a checkpoint
carries the id of the state it applies to and its own id is the hash of
its bytes, so the ids form a chain.

JS_ReadSnapshotChain() applies a sequence of checkpoints on top of a
base: the cells, atoms and strings of each one are numbered after the
previous ones, bodies are folded (a patch applies to the body left by
the previous checkpoint) and only then read. It rejects a missing,
reordered or plain delta inside the chain. When the last delta is a
chained checkpoint, the restored state is attached as the base, so the
restored runtime continues the chain. JS_ReadSnapshot() is now a
wrapper, and JS_GetSnapshotBaseId() gives the host the id to store with
a checkpoint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
